ring_kat exit 0 and crypto_instrument PASS on both (judge exit 0). No verdict row is registered (stage 3's).

What changed from round 1 (9a318695e, ../bench-*):
  - each row is built only after ours matched ring (AEAD/OpenSSH records and tags, SHA-2, HMAC, HKDF, Ed25519;
    ML-KEM against ml-kem), and ours's open/reject rows open ring's ciphertext; every check held on both benches
  - samples are printed exactly, so each row recomputes: recompute.py, an independent reading of stage 3's text,
    reproduces every printed spread, ratio and verdict of both builds on both benches (recompute.log: 0 mismatches)
  - each build records the ISA its feature detection admits (std's is_x86_feature_detected!, CPUID gated by
    OSXSAVE and XCR0), the same for both builds:
      the T14       aes,pclmulqdq,sha,movbe,bmi2,adx,avx,avx2,vaes,vpclmulqdq,avx512f,avx512vl
      the AMD bench aes,pclmulqdq,sha,movbe,bmi2,adx,avx,avx2
    Which path each crate took from these is still inferred from its detection code.
  - figures: every family's median and worst move by at most ~5% (T14 AES-GCM median 1.37 -> 1.43, the largest);
    verdicts on the shipped build: T14 70 fail, 1 remeasure, 3 pass, 3 excluded (was 68/3/3/3); AMD unchanged at
    73 fail, 1 pass, 3 excluded

bench-<b>/table.txt        the judge's table, ISA first; shipped columns | assertions-off columns (decide nothing;
                           compare "ratio off", not "ours ns off": ring moves between the two builds' runs too)
bench-<b>/headline.txt     per family: rows, median and worst ratio, verdict counts (shipped build)
